%T A398675 2689642694303500,5577118037055319531,15036379353504439695468,
%U A398675 51673939588399688953329600,222486324060410159568827595336,1182177984346438506689905220339385
%N A398675 Number of disconnected quasi-quintic graphs on 2*n + 1 vertices.
%C A398675 A quasi-quintic graph is a simple graph with one vertex of degree 6 and every other vertex of degree 5. By the handshaking lemma, it has odd order.
%C A398675 Let A_5(N), C_5(N), and R_5(N) count all quasi-quintic graphs, connected quasi-quintic graphs, and all quintic graphs on N vertices, respectively, with R_5(0) = 1. Unique component decomposition gives A_5(N) = Sum_j C_5(j)*R_5(N-j), and hence A_5(N)-C_5(N) = Sum_{j<N} C_5(j)*R_5(N-j).
%H A398675 Eric W. Weisstein, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/Quasi-QuinticGraph.html">Quasi-Quintic Graph</a>, MathWorld.
%F A398675 a(n) = A398640(n) - A398641(n). Also, a(n) = Sum_{j<2*n+1} C_5(j)*R_5(2*n+1-j).
%F A398675 G.f.: B(x)*(1 - 1/C(x)) where B(x) is the g.f. of A398640 and C(x) is the g.f. of A165626. - _Andrew Howroyd_, Aug 17 2026
%e A398675 a(10) = 1515471414 = 1*3459386 + 20*7849 + 3749*60 + 1877694*3 + 1505997026*1.
%Y A398675 Cf. A398640 (all quasi-quintic graphs), A398641 (connected quasi-quintic graphs), and A165626 (quintic graphs).
%K A398675 nonn,changed
